{{#is_alert}}A quarter of proxied upload parts failed over 30 minutes.{{/is_alert}}
{{#is_warning}}More than 5% of proxied upload parts failed over 30 minutes.{{/is_warning}}
The rate is failed parts over all parts, with the total floored at 20, so a handful of parts cannot trip it. Split `cyanotype.uploads.parts{outcome:error}` by `reason`: `client_aborted` and `body_too_short` are browsers or networks dropping mid-part (a flaky link, or a gateway timeout shorter than a slow upload), `storage_error` is the bucket refusing parts, `other` is everything else. The matching warn logs are `service:cyanotype-assets "part upload failed"` with `upload_id`, `part`, `reason`, `bytes_received`, `bytes_expected` and `elapsed_ms`.
